<title>EGYPT: Egypt cuts import tariff for some Lebanese apples.</title>
<headline>Egypt cuts import tariff for some Lebanese apples.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt has cut the import duty on a quota of Lebanese apples to 30 percent from 40 percent, the government newspaper al-Ahram said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The reduction applies to the first 18,500 tonnes of Lebanese apples imported into Egypt by January 31, 1997, it said, quoting a decree by Egyptian Prime Minister Kamal Ganzouri.</p>
<p>Lower tariffs for apples have traditionally been one of Lebanon's main requests in trade talks with Egypt.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
